    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d385-a2">

                <pb facs="0659" n="1619" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1619"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No.
                    129.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Said Pasha to Mr.
                            King.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Sublime Porte,<lb/>Ministry of Foreign
                            Affairs</hi></placeName>,<lb/><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-10-21"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 21,
                        1888</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chargé d’affaires</hi>: In answer to the note you
                    kindly addressed to me on the 22d of September last, No. 45, I have the honor to
                    inform you that the Sublime Porte having lately decided that the measure
                    concerning the Israelites going to Palestine shall not be applied but to those
                    who emigrate in number (<hi rendition="#italic">en nombre</hi>) and that no
                    obstacle shall be opposed to the sojourn of those who are not in this class, the
                    provisions with regard to the three Israelites, American citizens, who arrived
                    at Jaffa on the 20th of August last, have had to be withdrawn in consequence of
                    the instructions which have been forwarded in the foregoing sense to his
                    excellency Raouf Pacha.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Said.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
